    "title" : "Enforce Maximum Line Length",
    "description" : "This rule enforces a maximum allowed length for each line of code, typically limiting lines to 80 characters by default.",
    "explanation" : "This rule imposes a maximum line length on your code. <a\nhref=\"https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0008/\">Python's style\nguide</a> does a good job explaining why you might want to limit the\nlength of your lines, though this is a matter of taste.\n\nLines can be no longer than eighty characters by default.",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
