        "default" : "false",
        "description" : "Detect console statements"
      }
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "no_empty_functions",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Empty Functions",
    "description" : "This rule disallows declaring empty functions to prevent unintentional empty callbacks.",
    "explanation" : "Disallows declaring empty functions. The goal of this rule is that\nunintentional empty callbacks can be detected:\n<pre>\n<code>someFunctionWithCallback ->\ndoSomethingSignificant()\n</code>\n</pre>\nThe problem is that the call to\n<tt>doSomethingSignificant</tt> will be made regardless\nof <tt>someFunctionWithCallback</tt>'s execution. It can\nbe because you did not indent the call to\n<tt>doSomethingSignificant</tt> properly.\n\nIf you really meant that <tt>someFunctionWithCallback</tt>\nshould call a callback that does nothing, you can write your code\nthis way:\n<pre>\n<code>someFunctionWithCallback ->\n    undefined\ndoSomethingSignificant()\n</code>\n</pre>",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "no_empty_param_list",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Empty Parameter Lists in Function Definitions",
    "description" : "This rule prohibits defining functions with empty parameter lists.",
    "explanation" : "This rule prohibits empty parameter lists in function definitions.\n<pre>\n<code># The empty parameter list in here is unnecessary:\nmyFunction = () -&gt;\n\n# We might favor this instead:\nmyFunction = -&gt;\n</code>\n</pre>\nEmpty parameter lists are permitted by default.",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 1,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "no_implicit_braces",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Implicit Braces in Object Literals",
    "description" : "This rule forbids the use of implicit braces when declaring object literals in CoffeeScript.",
    "explanation" : "This rule prohibits implicit braces when declaring object literals.\nImplicit braces can make code more difficult to understand,\nespecially when used in combination with optional parenthesis.\n<pre>\n<code># Do you find this code ambiguous? Is it a\n# function call with three arguments or four?\nmyFunction a, b, 1:2, 3:4\n\n# While the same code written in a more\n# explicit manner has no ambiguity.\nmyFunction(a, b, {1:2, 3:4})\n</code>\n</pre>\nImplicit braces are permitted by default, since their use is\nidiomatic CoffeeScript.",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
      {
        "name" : "strict",
        "default" : "true",
        "description" : "Strict"
      }
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "no_implicit_parens",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Implicit Parentheses in Function Calls",
    "description" : "This rule forbids the use of implicit parentheses in function calls, requiring explicit parentheses instead.",
    "explanation" : "This rule prohibits implicit parens on function calls.\n<pre>\n<code># Some folks don't like this style of coding.\nmyFunction a, b, c\n\n# And would rather it always be written like this:\nmyFunction(a, b, c)\n</code>\n</pre>\nImplicit parens are permitted by default, since their use is\nidiomatic CoffeeScript.",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 2,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "no_interpolation_in_single_quotes",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Disallow Interpolation in Single Quoted Strings",
    "description" : "This rule prohibits the use of string interpolation inside single quoted strings in CoffeeScript.",
    "explanation" : "This rule prohibits string interpolation in a single quoted string.\n<pre>\n<code># String interpolation in single quotes is not allowed:\nfoo = '#{bar}'\n\n# Double quotes is OK of course\nfoo = \"#{bar}\"\n</code>\n</pre>\nString interpolation in single quoted strings is permitted by\ndefault.",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
